# Platform-managed agentplat state, not project source. In the
# client-initiated single-repo workspace layout (make's `Path: "."` spec) the
# repo root IS the workspace root, so these land inside this repo rather than
# beside it.
/.plugins/
/.opencode-skills/

# Exact Figma recovery archive; this is a backup, not active project source.
Follow Prompt Instructions.zip

# Local Netlify folder
.netlify

# Cloudinary media sync keeps its state and generated manifest in the repo
# on purpose (they stop two machines uploading the same file twice), so
# nothing is ignored here. Credentials live in .env.local, already ignored.

# Local original media. Every asset here is migrated to Cloudinary and served
# from there; the originals stay on disk as the rollback source. They are far
# too large for git — sitevideos/ alone is ~129 MB — so they are deliberately
# local-only. The generated manifest (src/media/manifest.json) and the upload
# mapping (media/sync-state.json) ARE tracked: the application and the sync
# both depend on them.
/sitevideos/
/caro images/

# Exact Figma design archive; a backup, not active project source.
Follow Design Instructions.zip
